All queries of the Galil DMC-41x3 driver now retry the empty or bare ``:`` replies that gclib
can return under rapid polling, instead of only ``is_in_motion`` and ``absolute_position``.
Non-empty replies that cannot be parsed, such as an absolute position with fewer than three
values, now raise immediately instead of being retried. ``GalilDMC4133Motor.on_off_status`` and
``off_when_error_occurs`` now parse the whole reply instead of only its first character.
``GalilMotionController.close`` now also closes the QCoDeS instrument, so a closed controller
can be created again with the same name.
